  "version": 1,
  "comments": {
    "c1": {
      "anchor": "context#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "1. Context",
      "excerpt": "Spell (English) Spanish Example Has today? Moment.js Temporal / Intl Notes or cl",
      "text": "also `the weekday`",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-18T02:39:58.479Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "the day of the week of now",
      "offset": 1486,
      "edited": "2026-11-18T02:40:42.407Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-18T03:04:06.965Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes:  <code>the weekday</code> and <code>the day of the week</code> both give Tuesday.  Recorded on T159.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "context#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "1. Context",
      "excerpt": "Spell (English) Spanish Example Has today? Moment.js Temporal / Intl Notes or cl",
      "text": "also `short day of the week` or `short weekday` for `Tue`",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-18T02:40:11.907Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Tuesday",
      "offset": 1542,
      "edited": "2026-11-18T02:40:49.720Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-18T03:04:10.589Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes:  <code>short weekday</code> and <code>short day of the week</code> give Tue.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "context#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "1. Context",
      "excerpt": "Spell (English) Spanish Example Has today? Moment.js Temporal / Intl Notes or cl",
      "text": "`the (AM or? PM|AMPM|meridian)` -- case insensitive",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-18T02:41:22.483Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "the AM or PM of now",
      "offset": 2848,
      "edited": "2026-11-18T02:42:12.680Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-18T03:04:13.830Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes, case-insensitive:  <code>the AM or PM of</code>, <code>the AMPM of</code>, <code>the meridiem of</code> and <code>meridian</code>, beside <code>if now is PM</code>.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c4": {
      "anchor": "context#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "1. Context",
      "excerpt": "Spell (English) Spanish Example Has today? Moment.js Temporal / Intl Notes or cl",
      "text": "this needs to be region specifc!",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-18T02:42:38.067Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "11/17/26",
      "offset": 3332,
      "edited": "2026-11-18T02:42:43.109Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-18T03:04:17.431Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes:  every format follows the person's region (11/17/26 in the US, 17/11/26 in Spain).</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c5": {
      "anchor": "context#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "1. Context",
      "excerpt": "Spell (English) Spanish Example Has today? Moment.js Temporal / Intl Notes or cl",
      "text": "short should not say the year if it's the same year",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-18T02:43:33.450Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Nov 17, 2026",
      "offset": 4195,
      "edited": "2026-11-18T02:43:40.412Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-18T03:04:20.330Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes:  a short date leaves out the year when it's this year.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c6": {
      "anchor": "context#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "1. Context",
      "excerpt": "Spell (English) Spanish Example Has today? Moment.js Temporal / Intl Notes or cl",
      "text": "short duration vs duration -- e.g. my example about `24 hours ago` vs `23 hours, 45 minutes` etc.\n\nShort duration should be sensitive to the time.\n\n`long duration` could be exact down to the second.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-18T02:45:22.605Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "duration",
      "offset": 7362,
      "edited": "2026-11-18T02:46:18.931Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-18T03:04:23.396Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes:  <code>as a short duration</code> rounds to the scale (about a day:  \"1 day ago\");  <code>as a long duration</code> is exact to the second.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c7": {
      "anchor": "clashes#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "1.1 The clashes, in plain words",
      "excerpt": "The day-of-the-week number changes from person to person. Mockup's draft tests t",
      "text": "not an actual clash if we know types?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-18T02:46:59.212Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "the second of",
      "offset": 287,
      "edited": "2026-11-18T02:46:59.979Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-18T03:04:26.252Z",
          "html": "<p>Right:  on a date the type is known, so <code>the second of now</code> is the date's part;  the plural is accepted too.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c8": {
      "anchor": "clashes#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "1.1 The clashes, in plain words",
      "excerpt": "The day-of-the-week number changes from person to person. Mockup's draft tests t",
      "text": "yeah, this does feel wierd.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-18T02:48:12.392Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "The month is a name in Spell",
      "offset": 1154,
      "edited": "2026-11-18T02:48:16.781Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-18T03:04:29.277Z",
          "html": "<p>Month and weekday now read alike:  month = April, short month = Apr, month number = 4;  weekday = Tuesday, short weekday = Tue, weekday number = 2.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c9": {
      "anchor": "countdown",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "2. The countdown, with the recommended words",
      "excerpt": "2. The countdown, with the recommended words",
      "text": "`left` = `time left` -- remember that we can do multi-word variables!",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-18T03:00:57.731Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "# Weekend Countdown\n                // How long until the weekend:  days, hours, minutes and seconds, ticking down every second.\n                weekend countdown is an app\n                \tits \"time\" is a date\n                \t\t// This moment:  set again every second, so the countdown redraws\n                \tevery second\n                \t\tset its time to now\n                \tit \"is the weekend\" if its time is a weekend day\n                \t\t// Saturday and Sunday in most places:  the person's region says\n                \tits \"left\" is the next weekend - its time\n                \t\t// A duration:  2 days, 3 hours, 4 minutes and 5 seconds\n                \tto draw it\n                \t\t<container text>\n                \t\t\t<segment padded=\"very\">\n                \t\t\t\t<if it is the weekend>\n                \t\t\t\t\t<header>It's the weekend!</header>\n                \t\t\t\t<else>\n                \t\t\t\t\t<text color=\"grey\">Weekend starts in</text>\n                \t\t\t\t\t<statistic \"Days\">{the days of its left}</statistic>\n                \t\t\t\t\t<statistic \"Hr\">{the hours of its left as two digits}</statistic>\n                \t\t\t\t\t<statistic \"Min\">{the minutes of its left as two digits}</statistic>\n                \t\t\t\t\t<statistic \"Sec\">{the seconds of its left as two digits}</statistic>\n                \t\t\t\t</if>\n                \t\t\t</segment>\n                \t\t</container>",
      "offset": 0,
      "edited": "2026-11-18T03:01:17.812Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-18T03:04:32.186Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes:  the countdown will say <code>time left</code>, and its other parts, as multi-word names.</p>"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "on": {}
}
